pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% THE OPPOSITE-VERDICT COMPANION, same formula and same binary. The formula has THREE
% solutions over its preserved set {x1,x2}; here they are, excluded one at a time with
% `solx`, after which the database really is contradicting and the enumeration really is
% complete. This is what `conclusion ENUMERATION_COMPLETE` is for, and it verifies before
% and after the fix — the fix only refuses the count when an OBJECTIVE-RESTRICTING
% constraint is doing the contradicting.
f 1 ;
solx x1 x2 ;
solx x1 ~x2 ;
solx ~x1 x2 ;
rup 1 ~x1 >= 1 ;
rup >= 1 ;
output NONE ;
conclusion ENUMERATION_COMPLETE 3 ;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
